\tag{fdip}
\title{States and pullback of observables}
\date{2026-10-23}

\p{An observable algebra records which quantities can be added and
multiplied; a normalized linear functional assigns them expectation
values. Here positivity is defined over #{\mathbb R} or #{\mathbb C}
with a specified involution. Finite
configuration sets make these choices explicit: functionals are weights,
and real or complex states are probability weights.}

\p{A supplied algebra map pulls a functional back by precomposition.
For a map of finite configurations this operation sums weights along
fibers; the sixteen configurations of a four-cycle give a nonuniform
example. Coordinate restriction also pulls polynomial functions back,
so any state already defined on the larger polynomial algebra restricts
to the retained one. Gaussian measures and their integrability enter
separately in [real actions and Gaussian states](fdip-0017).}

